ostrya-mountd (0.15.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * mount.ostrya and the daemon mount the image of a supplement
    composefs only if the commit carries ostree.composefs.digest.v0 and
    the digest of /root.cfs is the key. They do not compare the key for
    an attachment composefs.
  * With [ex-integrity] fsverity=yes, the object of /root.cfs must have
    an fs-verity seal. If the commit carries ostree.composefs.digest.v0,
    the digest of a built image must be the key.

 -- Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:32:20 +0100

ostrya-mountd (0.14.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The mount helper mount.ostrya runs for "mount -t ostrya". For root
    in the initial user namespace, it mounts the image of the commit in
    its own process. For each other caller, it asks the daemon.
  * The daemon mounts the image of the image commit that a commit names
    as the attachment composefs, or else as the supplement composefs.
    It reads no image file below extensions/ostrya/composefs. It refuses
    an image whose size is not a positive multiple of 4096 bytes.

 -- Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:05:49 +0100

